YOUR TASK: Complete this task: Implement the functional-graph counting solution in Python: read N, S, T; build target[26] and present[26], rejecting any source letter with two different target letters; compute bad_count, color_freq, and original indegree for bad edges to present targets; use Kahn topological removal to find nontrivial cycles and count a cycle as bare iff every vertex has original indegree 1; set spare = (present_count < 26) or (any color_freq[c] >= 2); print -1 if inconsistent or (bare_cycles > 0 and not spare), otherwise print bad_count + bare_cycles; run the provided samples.